schema SiteProgram
generation site-presentation-1
authority CMS + SurfaceIR + SitePresentation + InformationPolicy + CapabilityClosure

field program_id
  type text
  required true
  role stable-site-program-identity

field site_id
  type text
  required true
  role SitePresentation-reference

field experience_programs
  type set[text]
  required true
  role human-purpose-reference

field application_bindings
  type set[text]
  required true
  role typed-application-reference

field renderer_preferences
  type json
  required true
  role portable-interaction-renderer-tournament-input

field source_collections
  type set[text]
  required true
  role reagent-collection-reference

field capability_programs
  type set[text]
  required true
  role carrier-subprogram-reference

field actor_presentations
  type json
  required true
  role presentation-class-variation-only

field status
  type enum
  values draft published retired
  required true

invariant program-does-not-duplicate-site-identity
  statement subject, territory and Ghost profile resolve through SitePresentation; SiteProgram composes them and may not restate or override them

invariant program-requires-typed-application-edges
  statement each referenced application binding must name a typed ApplicationKind and each executable action remains behind its named native aperture

invariant renderer-is-portable
  statement renderer preferences choose interaction behavior only; a Pixelfed, Mobilizon, Lemmy, Zulip, Pinry, MapLibre, commerce or work grammar is never bound to one route or semantic owner

forbidden_inference SiteProgram renderer preference -> material existence, actor identity, authority, provider admission, payment, spend or effect
forbidden_inference SiteProgram source collection -> content, source rights, freshness or publication permission

invariant stage-needs-a-real-application
  statement each published stage names a typed application and material or capability transition; a prose chain token cannot be a stage

forbidden_inference ExperienceStage action -> authority, provider admission, payment authority or a completed effect
